    "tut.sales-return.title": "Processing a Return",
    "tut.sales-return.desc": "If a customer needs to return an item, use the return form. Enter the quantity to return and refund amount.",
    "tut.sales-return.instruction": "Click the return icon on any sale. Enter the quantity to return (max: original quantity). Set refund to 0 for exchange only. Provide a reason.",
    "tut.sales-detail-edit.title": "Editing a Transaction (Sale Detail)",
    "tut.sales-detail-edit.desc": "From the sale detail view, you can edit the customer info, quantity, discount, and VAT for any transaction.",
    "tut.sales-detail-edit.instruction": "Click the edit icon on a sale. Update the customer name, phone, quantity, discount, or VAT fields. Click Confirm to save changes.",
    "tut.sales-best-practices.title": "Sales Best Practices",
    "tut.sales-best-practices.desc": "Master these tips for accurate sales tracking.",
    "tut.sales-best-practices.instruction": "• Always verify quantities before completing a sale\n• Use credit sales sparingly and track debts\n• Generate receipts for every transaction\n• Reconcile daily sales with cash on hand\n• Review sales trends weekly to spot patterns",
    "tut.tutorial-sale-detail.title": "Sale Detail & Transaction Management",
    "tut.tutorial-sale-detail.desc": "Learn how to review completed sales, edit transactions, process returns, void sales, and print receipts.",
    "tut.sale-detail-welcome.title": "Sale Detail Overview",
    "tut.sale-detail-welcome.desc": "The Sale Detail screen shows everything about a single transaction: customer info, items purchased, payment details, and financial summary.",
    "tut.sale-detail-welcome.instruction": "This view is organized into cards. From top to bottom: Sale Info, Item Details, Financial Summary, and optional Payment History.",
    "tut.sale-detail-info.title": "Sale Information",
    "tut.sale-detail-info.desc": "The Sale Info card shows the transaction date, customer name and phone, payment method, and payment status.",
    "tut.sale-detail-info.instruction": "Check the customer name and payment status. If this is a credit sale, the due date is displayed here.",
    "tut.sale-detail-items.title": "Items Purchased",
    "tut.sale-detail-items.desc": "The Item Details table lists every product in the transaction with quantity, unit, unit price, and total.",
    "tut.sale-detail-items.instruction": "Review each item. The product names, quantities, and individual totals are shown for reference.",
    "tut.sale-detail-financial.title": "Financial Summary",
    "tut.sale-detail-financial.desc": "The Financial Summary shows the subtotal, discount applied, VAT, and the final total price.",
    "tut.sale-detail-financial.instruction": "Verify the discount and VAT amounts. For credit sales, the due amount is shown separately.",
    "tut.sale-detail-edit.title": "Editing the Transaction",
    "tut.sale-detail-edit.desc": "Click the Edit button to modify customer info, quantity, discount, or VAT. Changes are saved with a confirm.",
    "tut.sale-detail-edit.instruction": 'Click Edit (pencil icon). Update customer name, phone, quantity, discount, or VAT. Click "Confirm" to save changes or "Cancel" to discard.',
    "tut.sale-detail-return-void.title": "Returns & Voiding",
    "tut.sale-detail-return-void.desc": "Use the Return button (undo icon) to process customer returns. Use Void to cancel the entire sale.",
    "tut.sale-detail-return-void.instruction": "Return: Click the amber Return button, enter return quantity, refund amount, and reason. Void: Click the red Void Sale button and provide a reason.",
    "tut.sale-detail-best-practices.title": "Transaction Best Practices",
    "tut.sale-detail-best-practices.desc": "Keep accurate records with these tips.",
    "tut.sale-detail-best-practices.instruction": "• Always provide a receipt after completing a sale\n• Use returns instead of voiding when possible\n• Document void reasons clearly for audit trails\n• Verify customer identity for credit sale edits\n• Print receipts for customer records",
    "tut.tutorial-customers.title": "Customer Management",
